WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.970
 I'm going to show you how to
take this old dresser drawer

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.747
and turn it into a garden.

00:00:07.747 --> 00:00:09.080
NWA: (SINGING) Express yourself.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.860
I'm expressing with
my full capabilities.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.010
 There is no end to the
bounty of mother nature.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:16.650
There's enough for everybody,
and that's the one thing

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:20.620
that you will learn
from gardening.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.450
Most importantly, what
I'm going to teach

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.391
you is how to grow
your own food.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:26.690
(SINGING) Legendary.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:27.455
Whoa.

00:00:27.455 --> 00:00:29.080
 In this class what
you going to learn

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.170
is how to take some of my
favorite vegetables and herbs

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:36.010
from planting to harvesting,
mint, lettuce, sage,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.965
sweet potatoes, rosemary, kale.

00:00:37.965 --> 00:00:39.340
I know a lot of
people out there,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.730
you don't like leafy greens.

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.948
I don't either.

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:44.740
Put them in your diet,
anyway, because this

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.770
is one of the healthiest things
that you can possibly eat.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.180
You're going to
learn how to make

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.960
the most of any patch of soil,
from sidewalks to roof tops

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.130
to flower pots.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.260
And I know you're asking,
what the hell is compost?

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.620
Compost is one of the
sexiest things on the planet.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.020
This takes things out
of the waste cycle.

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.507
They don't wind up
in the landfill.

00:01:03.507 --> 00:01:05.590
(SINGING) Things ain't
never going to be the same.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:07.750
 These things are
really important,

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.526
not only to your garden,
but to the planet.

00:01:10.526 --> 00:01:12.170
(SINGING) Are you ready?

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.110
Are you ready?

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:15.090
 I call myself the
gangster gardener,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.700
'cause to me having
knowledge is gangster.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:18.780
Soil is gangster.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.410
Air is gangster as [BLEEP].

00:01:20.410 --> 00:01:21.620
(SINGING) Make way for me.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:24.180
 Gardens to me
represent freedom.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.720
That's one of the reasons that
I started growing food myself.

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.650
And I had no idea what happened
in my community,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.150
then around the world,
would happen just

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.367
from me planting a strip in
South Central Los Angeles.

00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:37.200
(SINGING) Legendary.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.550
Are you ready?

00:01:38.550 --> 00:01:41.820
 We are supposed to inspire
each other to wake up an--

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.610
and realize what's
truly important.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.890
I want to bring your
creativity into your space.

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:52.069
I want you to know that you
have the power to do this.

00:01:52.069 --> 00:01:53.130
(SINGING) Legendary.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.072
 I'm Ron Finley, and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:56.072 --> 00:01:57.030
(SINGING) Wait and see.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.530
Wait and see.

00:01:58.530 --> 00:01:59.930
They going to talk about me.

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.080
Just wait and see.

